WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.839
The Marvel Cinematic Universe is getting a
little smaller, as thousands of theaters around

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:07.640
the world decline to screen its recent movies.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.640
Here's why countries around the world are
apparently banning the series' new movies,

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.370
and what it might mean for the future of the
MCU.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:18.890
"Thor: Love and Thunder" is finally here,
and the film's early box office numbers indicate

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:22.750
that it's going to be another financial success
story for Marvel and Disney.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:27.070
According to The Numbers, Taika Waititi's
follow-up to "Thor: Ragnarok" gave the god

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:32.800
of thunder's solo franchise its biggest opening
to date, having made over $300 million after

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.730
its first weekend in theaters.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.580
That's a lot of dough for the space Viking.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:41.010
This is despite the fact that "Thor: Love
and Thunder" has divided critics and fans

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.010
alike.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.980
While some people enjoy the humorous take
on the Thor mythos, others feel like the movie

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.830
is too jokey for its own good.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.860
However, mixed reviews could be the least
of the film's concerns as it continues to

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.400
roll out in theaters worldwide.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.830
While "Thor: Love and Thunder" is shaping
up to be an international super hit, the movie

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:02.320
looks set to be banned in certain regions
that have been profitable for Hollywood blockbusters

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.460
in recent years.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.390
If the movie does indeed face the chopping
block in these regions, it will mark yet another

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:10.920
Disney release to be banned for the same reason
in 2022.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.940
"Let's bring the rainbow."

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.500
"'Bring the rainbow,' is that her catchphrase
or something?"

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.510
"Thor: Love and Thunder" is the latest Disney
release to feature brief moments of LGBTQ

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:26.770
representation, which could prevent the movie
from being granted a release in China and

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:27.980
other territories.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:32.360
The latest Marvel release implies that Valkyrie
is bisexual, with her mentioning she had a

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.909
girlfriend back in the day.

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:38.710
It also reveals that Korg is effectively gay,
being a part of a species that only has one

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:39.710
gender.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:43.270
Industry experts believe that these aspects
will be enough to stop the movie from being

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.880
released in certain regions.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:50.020
Taika Waititi and Natalie Portman have also
been celebrating the LGBTQ aspects of "Thor:

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.620
Love and Thunder," with the pair having recently
described the movie as, quote, "so gay," and

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.250
quote, "super gay," at a Q&amp;A and screening.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:01.630
However, they were subsequently criticized
by Marvel fans as scenes involving positive

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:06.700
LGBTQ representation in the movie are actually
few and far between, which is unfortunate

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:11.600
considering the film is reported to have originally
included a significant romantic scene involving

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.470
Valkyrie that was cut, presumably to appease
censors.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:19.160
It's an unfortunate happenstance, especially
seeing as how Valkyrie was supposed to have

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.380
her sexuality play a more prominent role in
"Thor: Ragnarok," but that ended up getting

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.380
cut, as well.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:28.690
If the situation follows the same trajectory
as "Lightyear," which includes a same-gender

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.640
kissing scene, "Thor: Love and Thunder" could
also be banned in territories such as the

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.020
Middle East, Malaysia, and Indonesia.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:39.240
Reportedly, the Disney-Pixar release is currently
banned in 14 countries.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.240
"Flick!"

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.040
"Okay, we should go."

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.600
"Thor: Love and Thunder" isn't the first Marvel
film to have an issue getting released in

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.959
other countries, and if current trajectories
are any indication, it certainly won't be

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:52.959
the last.

00:02:52.959 --> 00:02:57.720
Phase 4 of the Marvel Cinematic Universe has
been faced with bans around the globe, particularly

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.780
when it came to the release of "Eternals."

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:05.120
That film faced bans in Kuwait, Qatar, and
Saudi Arabia due to the inclusion of a same-sex

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.120
relationship.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.220
In that movie, Phastos is married to a man
named Ben, and the two share a kiss.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:15.250
Homosexuality is banned through much of the
region, and movies depicting LGBTQ relationships

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.780
tend to get banned.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:20.720
That was the case with the most recent Marvel
flick before "Thor 4" — "Doctor Strange

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.250
in the Multiverse of Madness."

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:27.140
That film was banned in the same countries,
seemingly due to America Chavez' parents being

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.720
in a lesbian relationship.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.140
Additionally, those movies, as well as "Shang-Chi
and the Legend of the Ten Rings" were banned

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.180
in China for various reasons.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.830
It remains to be seen if the next movie in
the MCU, "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever,"

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:43.849
will make its way to China's shores, but things
aren't looking hopeful.

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:48.280
Despite that, these movies seem to still be
making plenty of money no matter what.

